feov-record: merge: record: verdict requires --as PASS|FAIL (got "banana") — a PASS is checked against the open board by exact match, so any other spelling skips the check entirely and records an unadjudicated pass

── outcome in the wrong case
exit 2
feov-record: bench: record: outcome requires --as VERIFIED|CEILING|HALTED|UNVERIFIED (got "ceiling") — "ceiling" differs from "CEILING" only in case, and the report's verdict stamp switches on this word — an unrecognized one falls through to a bare stamp, so a lowercase CEILING loses the "this is NOT a judged failure to verify" caveat the stamp exists to carry

── petition ruling outside the set
exit 2
feov-record: bench: record: petition-rule requires --as granted|denied (got "halt") — relief binds the coming seats only on an exact `granted`, so a near-miss grants nothing while reading as a grant on the record — and a halt is the bench's own verb, which this set closing is what actually makes true

